# ABOUTME: Reserves the paths that define this repo's own constraints.
# ABOUTME: Adapted from controls/approval-gating/server-side/CODEOWNERS, which is the template.
#
# The github-actions-pipeline example argues that a CI agent's constraints are
# files it can propose changing, so the only real control is the forge. This
# file is that argument applied to this repo: a change to the workflow surface,
# to the checks, or to the licence split needs a named reviewer.
#
# Single maintainer today, so this is attribution and intent rather than a
# second pair of eyes. It becomes enforcement the moment a second contributor
# exists, and it is what verify.sh looks for.

*                       @peopleforrester

# The loop the pipeline example is about: the constraints themselves.
/.github/                @peopleforrester
/.githooks/              @peopleforrester
/scripts/                @peopleforrester

# The data the site and the checks read as source of truth.
/data/                   @peopleforrester

# Claims that have to survive scrutiny.
/framework/CITATIONS.md  @peopleforrester
/framework/ASSURANCE.md  @peopleforrester
/framework/BYPASSES.md   @peopleforrester

# Licence split.
/LICENSE                 @peopleforrester
/LICENSE-CONTENT         @peopleforrester
